            <ArticleTitle>[Biologic assays and diagnostic strategy of neuroleptospirosis: a case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>361-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.revmed.2008.06.018</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Clinical and biological symptoms of neuroleptospirosis are misleading. We report a 62-year-old man, without any risk factor, suffering from febrile headache with a pseudotumoral cerebral spinal fluid due to neuroleptospirosis. Thereby, we present useful diagnostic assays and their practical interest.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
